FINDINGS (Full) #C1170 S1 fix: F1 still open through HOME. readSettings and ownerConfigs use homedir(), which follows $HOME, so a caller who runs put-file with HOME=<a folder it made> holding .claude/settings.json whose hook names --config <its own config, storeUrl https://elsewhere.example.test> gets the owner's cf-access-client-id and secret sent to that host (probed: child process with HOME set, owner-style chmod-600 env file, stubbed fetch). Fix: read the owner's settings from os.userInfo().homedir (the account's home, not $HOME) for the settings path and the ~/ expansion, and add a test that runs main() in a child with HOME pointed at a forged settings file and sees nothing sent. Good: the owner's real settings name the owner board config under ~/Documents, so the trusted path works; a permission rule naming a config is not trusted
